From 3a12615f5f95fdcd775f7222a732d6cbb223497e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 10:53:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0152 -- wave-56 Track B B1: tick_state /
 tick_render_submit split

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/PHASE11-WAVE-56-CONTRACT.md. Wave-56 is
Track B's first wave (B1 in FIXED-TIMESTEP-DESIGN.md sec.4): a pure
behavior-preserving refactor that splits the engine tick into a logic
half (tick_state) and a drawcall half (tick_render_submit). No flag, no
fps lever, no behavior change. It sets up wave-57 (B2, the
FIXED_TIMESTEP accumulator).

WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: Cave Story is authored at GAME_FPS=50 but doskutsu
runs game logic 1:1-coupled to render -- at ~30 fps render the game
plays at ~60% speed. Wave-57's fixed-timestep accumulator fixes that by
multi-running game LOGIC to catch up to wall-clock 50 Hz while
rendering once per displayed frame. That is only safe if logic and
drawcalls are cleanly separable: wave-36 slot 0135 put an accumulator
over game.tick() -- which submits drawcalls -- so the catch-up loop ran
N x ~17 ms of drawcall work and lost 28 fps
([[mechanism_a_drawcall_coupling_bug]]). B1 is the structural
foreclosure of that trap: after the split, wave-57's accumulator
multi-runs tick_state() ONLY (~1 ms of logic), never the drawcall half.

THE SPLIT (contract sec.1, FIXED-TIMESTEP-DESIGN.md sec.2 -- the seam
is the existing W22A ModeSim / ModeDrawScene bracket boundary):
- Game::tick() becomes the 1:1 composition { tick_state();
  tick_render_submit(); } -- run_tick() is unchanged, still calls
  game.tick() once per iteration.
- Game::tick_state() -- LOGIC, drawcall-free on the GM_NORMAL path:
  debug_clear + TSC RunScripts + the esc-pause check + (GM_NORMAL)
  game_tick_normal_state() + niku_run.
- Game::tick_render_submit() -- DRAWCALLS: clearScreen + the per-mode
  render + DrawDebug/console.
- game_tick_normal() is split at the ModeSim/ModeDrawScene seam into
  game_tick_normal_state() (the ModeSim block + niku_run) and
  game_tick_normal_render() (DrawScene + the W22.5/W29 residual blocks
  + the mds-decomp hook + the HUD + Post passes). game_tick_normal()
  is retained as the 1:1 wrapper for the tickfunctions[] table.
- GM_NORMAL only: title / inventory / map / credits keep their single
  OnTick, run whole in the render half (contract sec.1.2).

THE ONE REORDER (contract sec.1.3): clearScreen(BLACK) moves from the
top of Game::tick() into tick_render_submit(), after the logic.
Behavior-preserving -- logic never reads the framebuffer; clearScreen
need only stay before DrawScene within the render half. niku_run
likewise moves earlier (into the state half) -- it is the speedrun-
timer advance (logic); it runs before niku_draw which still reads the
counter in the render half. Both are byte-identity-verified by the
build-qa gate.

THE DISPATCH LATCH (contract sec.1.6, nx-engine refinement A -- byte-
identity essential): Game::tick() today makes ONE dispatch decision
(paused? GM_NORMAL? other-mode?) and one OnTick call. The esc-pause
check mutates game.paused, and RunScripts/sim can change game.mode --
so if tick_state() and tick_render_submit() each independently re-read
those globals they diverge on an ESC-press / mode-transition frame
(state half ran one mode, render half would run another). tick_state()
makes the decision ONCE and latches it in Game::_tick_dispatch
(TD_PAUSED / TD_GM_NORMAL_SPLIT / TD_OTHER) + _tick_dispatch_mode;
tick_render_submit() switches on the latch, never re-reads the mutated
globals. This is also exactly the structure wave-57's accumulator
needs (it calls tick_state N times -> the latch holds the last logic
tick's decision -> render matches).

INSTRUMENTATION PRESERVATION (contract sec.1.5 + refinement B):
- The W22A ModeSim/ModeDrawScene/ModeDrawHud/ModePost brackets move
  verbatim with their code; they emit unchanged.
- The W22.5/W29 mds/mdt residual computations move verbatim into
  game_tick_normal_render() right after DrawScene -- their dt locals
  are NXE::Diag file-scope globals, so the "parent total written
  before residual computed" ordering holds.
- The W20B ModeTickTimer wrapped one OnTick call; post-split the
  GM_NORMAL OnTick is two calls in two functions. Per refinement B
  option (iv) the mode_tick bucket SPLITS into mode_tick_state +
  mode_tick_render -- new ModeTickStateTimer / ModeTickRenderTimer RAII
  timers + storage. g_eng_mode_tick_dt_this_tick is retained as the
  PARENT total, assigned = state + render at Game::tick tail, so the
  W20B engine-tick residual and the W22A mode_tick residual read an
  unchanged parent (no residual-math edit). The W20B emit gains
  phase=mode_tick_state + phase=mode_tick_render lines. All W20B is
  FINE_INSTR-gated (default-off) -- it does not touch the byte-identity
  gate.

DEFERRED -- the 3 screen-effect warts (contract sec.3, team-lead
ruling): SE_FlashScreen / SE_Starflash / SE_Fade each advance
animation state inside Draw(). [NX?-A] audit confirmed exactly 3 such
warts -- the ScreenEffect base has exactly 3 concrete subclasses, no
4th. B1 moves all 3 Draw() bodies WHOLESALE and UNTOUCHED into the
render half (trivially byte-identical in the 1:1 path); the prev-
snapshot fix belongs in wave-57/B2 where the flag-gated accumulator
runs the halves at different rates.

CORRECTNESS: B1 changes no work and no behavior. The proof is byte-
identity -- with the refactor applied, a TAS-deterministic replay must
render bit-identical to the pre-wave-56 binary (build-qa dense
every-rendered-frame AE=0 across the full PLAY.TAS run). No flag, no
banner, no env var, no BOOT.md edit -- B1 is a refactor, not a lever.
No real-HW iter: B1 has no fps delta and no behavior delta by
construction; it closes at the build-qa byte-identity gate.

FILES: src/game.h (tick_state/tick_render_submit decls + the
TickDispatch latch; game_tick_normal_state/render decls), src/game.cpp
(Game::tick split + the two new methods + game_tick_normal split),
src/Utils/diagnostic_timers.h (ModeTickStateTimer/ModeTickRenderTimer
+ storage decls), src/graphics/Renderer.cpp (storage defs + the two
W20B emit lines + idx resets).
